@page
@using AuthMd.Sample.Service
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Home";
}

<h1>Sample Notes</h1>
<p>
    An ordinary ASP.NET Core Identity app that AI agents can register with on behalf of its users,
    through the <a href="/auth.md">auth.md</a> protocol.
</p>

<h2>Try it</h2>
<ol>
    <li>Leave this app running.</li>
    <li>In another terminal, start the agent: <code>dotnet run --project samples/AuthMd.Sample.Agent</code></li>
    <li>The agent prints a link and a 6-digit code. Open the link.</li>
    <li>Sign in as <code>@DemoUser.Email</code> with password <code>@DemoUser.Password</code>.</li>
    <li>Type the code and approve. The agent picks up from there.</li>
</ol>
<p>
    To try it as someone with no account, give the agent another email:
    <code>dotnet run --project samples/AuthMd.Sample.Agent -- http://localhost:5125/ you@example.com</code>.
    Then choose <a href="/Account/Register">Create one</a> on the sign-in page and sign up with that email.
</p>

<h2>What agents read</h2>
<ul>
    <li><a href="/auth.md">/auth.md</a>: the instructions</li>
    <li><a href="/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource">/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource</a></li>
    <li><a href="/.well-known/oauth-authorization-server">/.well-known/oauth-authorization-server</a></li>
</ul>
